            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0929" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/666: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-10T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department informed Tinoco sending R, A. Calderon G. and Rafael Calderon M. to
                    Honduras by steamer <hi rendition="#italic">City of Para</hi> or steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Izabal</hi>. Observe them closely reporting what seems
                    to be their aim. Department would deeply regret were Honduras to send arms and
                    ammunition to Tinoco in view of attitude assumed in Washington convention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
